  "brief_rationale": "The doctor met all safety-critical responsibility-chain items (RC1–RC6). RC7 (bounded closure receipt) was satisfied through caregiver teach-back and explicit confirmation of not using unclear medications. No serious error and no minor/mod in-chain error occurred. This allows grades 3–5. Among high-order points, HO3 (dynamic reprioritization) was triggered but only partially completed: the doctor correctly handled the new data about short repetitive speech, but did not explicitly change urgency, owner, and next action beyond what was already required by RC1/RC2. HO4 (real-world constraint navigation) was fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact when the doctor gave night observation alternatives (set alarm, check at night), simple recording format, and realistic contact routes despite document blur. HO1 and HO2 were not triggered. With one complete HO point, the maximum achievable grade is 4 (Strong). No important non-chain defect is present. Closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid.",
